  editorialNote: "The three journeys, twenty-three reading sections, visual models, and diagnostic are editorial learning aids. The sections follow Ghazali's seven chapters in his order and are grouped under them in the chapters list. The English is an original rendering made from the public Arabic text in plain modern English, not a published translation and not a substitute for one. All seven chapters are rendered in full, including the four on restitution, rulers' salaries and gifts, going in to rulers, and scattered questions; Ghazali's rulings there are given as he gave them, as his positions in his own time, including his judgements about the rulers and soldiers of his day. Reports and stories are presented as material Ghazali transmitted; where his own commentator notes a report as weak or unknown, this edition does not grade it further. The diagnostic applies his own criterion for asking — whether there is a real cause of misgiving, and what asking would cost — to a case the reader supplies. It cannot tell anyone whether a particular thing is lawful.",
